Moleman wrote:

> ... but when I went to a different store to get
> more money I noticed there was a grave Inside a
> store. It read: "xxxx, killed by holy water". I
> wandered how on earth can you get killed by holy
> water?

> Then I started s)earching for mimics as I always
> do in store,

_Never_ search in a store. What do you hope to find?

There are no traps, no hidden doors.

Use "rest on '.'" instead.

The only thing you can find by searching is trouble,
in the form of a mimic that notices it has been
discovered, and wants to kill you for your efforts.

Walk only where your pet walks. Where it won't walk
are either mimics or cursed items. Don't borrow
trouble, don't go there.

  I tend to turn on autopickup, follow my pet from
  cell to cell, stepping only where I've seen, not
  deduced, that my pet stepped, thereby picking up
  stuff that is known to be uncursed, marked to be
  unpaid, and known not to be a mimic. Then I can
  retreat to a convenient corner, try on most of the
  armor, except pointy hats or unusual helms, #name
  everything marked unpaid individually as Uncursed,
  drop it all in a pile and go back to following in
  my pet's footsteps.

  [This has the nice side effect of stacking unpaid
  stuff in a pile useful for credit cloning, if you
  go for credit cloning.]

> and yes, next to me was a giant mimic (so that's
> what the holy water was...).

That combination is a _really_ unusual thing to find
in a shop.

> Giant mimic hits. All my 23 HP's were gone in one
> turn.  DYWYPI?

If you really, really want to find all the mimics
before exploring the store, carry in a handful of
rocks or glass or worthless darts or arrows or
unhelpful helms, let your pet identify for you safe
places to stand first (so you don't find a mimic
right next to you again) then throw items down each
row or column to make sure the grid cells the thrown
items cross aren't occupied by mimics.

If you do find a mimic, retreat out of the store
until you cannot see the mimic. Most times the
mimic, unwatched, will revert to mimicking some
object, most often a boulder, and you'll notice it
flash into view as you step back to the shop door,
telling you exactly where the mimic is. If that
doesn't work, back slowly out of the shop, letting
the mimic follow you clear to another room and well
into that room, then walk around the mimic and back
to the shop.

> Mimics are a real problem when I'll try not to
> level up, but I still need to go to stores to get
> money for protection.

They're only a problem if you annoy them by
searching or bumping into them.

> I'll usually try maneuvering around them if my pet
> doesn't kill them, which is usually the case.

Pets won't attack monsters (more than?) two hit dice
bigger than they are, the odds of dying are too
great.

Mostly, your cats and dogs need to be large cats and
large dogs before they'll take on a large mimic, and
even then a win is not guaranteed.

> Doesn't my pet see [the] mimic?

Sure, but your pet has an appropriate inborn
humility, too, and doesn't look for trouble it can't
handle, at least not too often.

